(RAW MATERIAL SUPPLY AGREEMENT) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THIS AGREEMENT is made on 1 March 2024 BETWEEN:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(1\) MWANGI FOODS LIMITED, a company incorporated in Kenya under) Tj T*
(    company number C.12/2011, whose registered office is at) Tj T*
(    Enterprise Road, Industrial Area, Nairobi \("the Company"\); and) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(2\) KABRAS SUGAR LIMITED, whose registered office is at) Tj T*
(    Malava, Kakamega \("the Counterparty"\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(RECITALS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The Company wishes to procure refined white sugar meeting KEBS KS EAS 4.) Tj T*
(B. The Counterparty has represented that it is able and willing to) Tj T*
(   provide the same on the terms set out below.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. DEFINITIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1.1 "Services" means refined white sugar meeting KEBS KS EAS 4.) Tj T*
(1.2 "Business Day" means a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or a) Tj T*
(    public holiday in Kenya.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. TERM AND RENEWAL) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.1 This Agreement commences on 1 March 2024 \(the Effective Date\)) Tj T*
(    and expires on 28 February 2026 unless terminated earlier under) Tj T*
(    clause 7.) Tj T*
(2.2 The term shall renew automatically for successive periods of twelve) Tj T*
(    \(12\) months unless either party gives ninety \(90\) days written) Tj T*
(    notice of non-renewal before the expiry date.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. CONSIDERATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.1 The total contract value is KES 2,500,000 exclusive of VAT.) Tj T*
(3.2 Payment shall be made within 75 days of a valid invoice.) Tj T*
(3.3 Late payment attracts interest at 2% per month.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. OBLIGATIONS OF THE COUNTERPARTY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4.1 The Counterparty shall deliver the Services at Nairobi.) Tj T*
(4.2 The Counterparty shall maintain product liability insurance of not) Tj T*
(    less than KES 10,000,000 throughout the term.) Tj T*
(4.3 The Counterparty shall submit a quarterly performance report within) Tj T*
(    fourteen \(14\) days of each quarter end.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. CONFIDENTIALITY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5.1 Each party shall keep confidential all information disclosed by the) Tj T*
(    other and shall not use it other than for this Agreement.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. LIABILITY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6.1 Neither party excludes liability for death, personal injury or) Tj T*
(    fraud. Otherwise each party liability is capped at the total) Tj T*
(    consideration paid in the preceding twelve months.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. TERMINATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7.1 Either party may terminate on ninety \(90\) days written notice.) Tj T*
(7.2 Either party may terminate immediately on the insolvency of the) Tj T*
(    other or on a material breach not remedied within thirty \(30\) days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8.1 This Agreement is governed by the laws of Kenya and the parties) Tj T*
(    submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Kenya.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9. STAMP DUTY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9.1 Any stamp duty payable under the Stamp Duty Act \(Cap 480\) shall be) Tj T*
(    borne by the Counterparty.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
